{
  "_comment": "Per-(stem, preset) drift: `mlx-community/NVIDIA-Nemotron-3-Super-120B-A12B-OptiQ-2bit` is an OptiQ mixed-bit checkpoint. Its section default is this preset's own 4-bit / g64 affine, and its `quantization` block lists every quantized module on its own — 354 per-module entries, copied here verbatim and in the checkpoint's order (291 at 4-bit, 63 at 2-bit; the router gate, conv1d, A_log, D, dt_bias, the norms and the correction bias are absent, i.e. dense). 4-bit: embeddings, lm_head, the Mamba in/out_proj, q/k/v/o, the shared experts and the latent projections. Routed experts (`switch_mlp.fc1`/`fc2`): 4/4 on layers 1 3 5 79 81 83 85 87, 2/2 on every MoE layer 10..76, and 4/2 on layer 8 — one bundle, two widths. A per-module map is authoritative (an unlisted module is dense), so this map alone decides every width the build reads; the dense nvidia base carries none of it. It cannot live in an arch-wide preset (#202: the per-role bit map is part of the fingerprint and dedup signature, and an arch-wide map makes every other checkpoint of the arch unloadable). What keeps this variant apart from a uniform one at load time is the per-role affine bit map in `fingerprint_matches`, whose rows list the routed experts per layer. `crates/models/quantization/test_fixtures/` carries the checkpoint's config.json verbatim; a macro unit test pins this map to it.",
